{
  "step1_summary": "• Chief complaint: 3-day history of persistent diarrhoea.\n• Symptom details:  – Diarrhoea: watery, no visible blood, urges every ~10 minutes; neither improving nor worsening.  – Abdominal pain: central/peri-umbilical, mild-to-moderate, relieved somewhat after bowel motion; mild tenderness on self-palpation.  – Vomiting: one episode this morning after eating fruit; no haematemesis.  – Nausea present; no reported fever (only mild sweating, unsure).  – No chest pain, no dyspnoea beyond baseline asthma, able to walk/talk.  – Not drinking much, limiting food intake. \n• Past medical history: Asthma.\n• Medications: Regular inhaler (brand recently changed); no other drugs reported.\n• Allergies: NKDA.\n• Family history: Father died of bowel (colorectal) cancer 10 years ago.\n• Social history: Employed; currently staying home due to symptoms. Smoking/alcohol not discussed.\n• Vital signs: Not provided.\n• Examination findings (remote): Patient-reported mild central abdominal tenderness; no red-flag peritonism described.\n• Labs/Imaging: None performed or reported.",
